= Culinary Publication

In the era of the dead internet it's hard for any media to have a reach without megacorp protection.  Among the street food vendors of Mikasa, a decentralized alternative exists.  Holographic data on the wrappers embed various media, jokes, stories, short clips and a bit of citizen journalism.  Depending who you ask this practice is Laisvė, Merdeka, Kūʻokoʻa, Inkululeko or dozens of other names with two meanings.

With so little unfiltered news that is safe from AI distortion during transmission, these publications have a surprisingly large readership.  They offer a tangible way to get or keep ideas into the public conciousness.  What ideas are people chewing on while they eat lunch today?

- @labor
- @otherworld
- @wealthy
- @diplomatic
- @return

@labor
title: Horror stories about the big 3
subtitle: Popular among the poor and pisses off nobody but the megacorps
choose-if: month_actions_remaining > 0 and anti_corp_media < 3
unavailable-subtitle: No organizing actions left this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spendProfessionalActionWithFallback();
Q.anti_corp_media += 1;
!}

Populist rhetoric is an easy way to get people wanting change.  The Stakeholder revolt might have been crushed but plenty of people are stakeholders in everything but name.  Today's snacks lean hard into shop-floor horror stories between the cat gifs.

@otherworld
title: Accounts from the Otherworld
subtitle: Humanize the non-humans — ease xenophobia
view-if: otherworld_media = 0
choose-if: month_actions_remaining > 0
unavailable-subtitle: No organizing actions left this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spendProfessionalActionWithFallback();
Q.otherworld_media += 1;
Q.parochialism = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.parochialism) || 0) - 1);
if (typeof Q.update_projections === 'function') { Q.update_projections() }
!}

Even in a place like Mikasa that is closer to the Otherworld than most, there are numerous misconceptions about Otherworlders.  Tales about what life is really like in the Otherworld fascinate many people and counteract harmful prejudices.

@wealthy
title: Self sufficiency and the needs of local businesses
subtitle: High skilled workers and cooperatives would like this but the establishment tone would be offputting to workers
view-if: self_sufficiency_media = 0
choose-if: month_actions_remaining > 0
unavailable-subtitle: No organizing actions left this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spendProfessionalActionWithFallback();
Q.self_sufficiency_media += 1;
!}

Terrestrials or Martians might be surprised that debates on IP restrictions for agrinutritional growth mediums can draw an broad audience but the topic is literally a matter of life and death in some parts of the city.  The wealthy are usually hostile towards the cooperatives but the discussion creates some cross-class solidarity, at least among the non-shareholders.  Anyone who needs to eat today has a stake in there being food tomorrow.

@diplomatic
title: Mikasa's place in the solar system economy and negotiations with megacorps
subtitle: We might be able to negotiate with corps in good faith, but any economic compromise would undermine self sufficiency
view-if: kiss_ass_media = 0
choose-if: month_actions_remaining > 0
unavailable-subtitle: No organizing actions left this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spendProfessionalActionWithFallback();
Q.kiss_ass_media += 1;
!}

Most people aren't interested in solarpolitical theory crafting but the podcast crowd keeps talking about it.  It doesn't move the needle on public opinion but maybe some good ideas will emerge from it.
